---
layout: base.njk
title: Woven Web
home: true
bodyClass: home
---

{%- macro weft(cls) -%}
<svg class="hero__weft {{ cls }}" viewBox="0 0 1200 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  {{ caller() }}
</svg>
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- set w1 = "M0,40 C260,22 470,62 760,42 S1080,26 1200,40" -%}
{%- set w2 = "M0,63 C230,80 560,36 830,60 S1090,74 1200,58" -%}
{%- set w3 = "M0,51 C190,42 400,72 640,52 S990,34 1200,56" -%}

<header class="hero">
  <div class="hero__inner">
  <h1 class="hero__name">
    {% call weft("hero__weft--under") %}
      <path class="w w1" d="{{ w1 }}" pathLength="1"/><path class="w w2" d="{{ w2 }}" pathLength="1"/><path class="w w3" d="{{ w3 }}" pathLength="1"/>
    {% endcall %}
    <span class="hero__word">Woven Web</span>
    {% call weft("hero__weft--over hero__weft--odd") %}
      <path class="w w1" d="{{ w1 }}" pathLength="1"/>
      <path class="w w3" d="{{ w3 }}" pathLength="1"/>
    {% endcall %}
    {% call weft("hero__weft--over hero__weft--even") %}
      <path class="w w2" d="{{ w2 }}" pathLength="1"/>
    {% endcall %}
  </h1>
  <p class="hero__lab">community research lab</p>
  <p class="hero__tagline">Weaving education, arts, and technology in service of life.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="sec" id="who" aria-labelledby="who-h">
  <h2 class="sec__title" id="who-h">Who we are</h2>
  <div class="sec__body prose">
    <p>Woven Web is a community research lab. We are fostering connected cultures, developing systems in support of life, and nurturing the intersection of education, arts, and technology.</p>
    <p>We are perhaps easiest to understand through our relationships — through the organizations and initiatives we are in collaboration with, and through the work we are doing together. We are rooted in Boulder, Colorado and woven into something larger.</p>
    <p class="prose__turn">The name says something true about our orientation: not <em>weaving</em> web, but <em>woven</em> web — recognizing the state of already being woven. The connections are already here. Our work is learning to see them, tend them, and build on them.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec sec--cohere" id="cohere" aria-labelledby="cohere-h">
  <h2 class="sec__title" id="cohere-h">COhere Boulder</h2>
  <div class="sec__body cohere">
    <p class="cohere__line"><span class="ph">[Aaron/Eileen: one line on COhere]</span></p>
    <figure class="cohere__quote">
      <blockquote><p>An ongoing community weaving process creating resilience through connection.</p></blockquote>
      <figcaption><a href="https://cohereboulder.org">cohereboulder.org</a></figcaption>
    </figure>
    <ol class="cohere__years" aria-label="Gatherings">
      <li>October 2024</li>
      <li>October 2025</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="web" aria-labelledby="web-h">
  <div class="band__inner">
    <div class="band__head">
      <h2 class="band__title" id="web-h">The woven web</h2>
      <p class="band__note">An early sketch of the web we're part of.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="web" data-web>
      <div class="web__places">
        <h3 class="web__label">Places where the culture is emerging</h3>
        {%- set v = wovenWeb.wide %}
        {% include "web-map.njk" %}
        {%- set v = wovenWeb.narrow %}
        {% include "web-map.njk" %}
        <p class="web__caption" id="web-caption" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="web__scenes">
        <h3 class="web__label">Scenes that overlap</h3>
        <ul class="bridges">
          {%- for b in wovenWeb.bridges %}
          <li>
            <button type="button" class="bridge" data-bridge="{{ b.id }}"{% if b.place %} data-place="{{ b.place }}"{% endif %} aria-pressed="false">
              <svg class="braid" viewBox="0 0 {{ wovenWeb.braid.W }} {{ wovenWeb.braid.H }}" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <defs><clipPath id="over-{{ b.id }}">
                  {%- for o in wovenWeb.braid.over %}<rect x="{{ o.x }}" y="0" width="{{ o.w }}" height="{{ wovenWeb.braid.H }}"/>{% endfor -%}
                </clipPath></defs>
                <path class="dye-{{ b.A.dye }}" d="{{ wovenWeb.braid.a }}"/>
                <path class="dye-{{ b.B.dye }}" d="{{ wovenWeb.braid.b }}"/>
                <path class="dye-{{ b.A.dye }}" d="{{ wovenWeb.braid.a }}" clip-path="url(#over-{{ b.id }})"/>
              </svg>
              <span class="bridge__names"><span>{{ b.A.name }}</span> <span><span class="bridge__x">×</span> {{ b.B.name }}</span></span>
            </button>
          </li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="relationships" aria-labelledby="rel-h">
  <h2 class="sec__title" id="rel-h">Our relationships</h2>
  <div class="sec__body relationships">

    <article class="relationship">
      <h3>Spirit of the Front Range</h3>
      <p>A newly forming 501(c)(3) focused on fostering a more connected bioregional network across the Front Range. We are closely partnered in building the infrastructure of belonging for this region.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="relationship">
      <h3>Regen Hub</h3>
      <p>A co-working and venture cooperative in downtown Boulder where much of our work lives and breathes. The Hub is a node — a place where builders, thinkers, and community weavers find each other.</p>
      <p class="relationship__links"><a href="https://regenhub.xyz">regenhub.xyz</a></p>
    </article>

    <article class="relationship">
      <h3>techne.institute</h3>
      <p>An integral technology institute we are helping to birth — bringing together AI, contemplative practice, and applied learning. Techne asks what it means to develop human capability alongside technological capability.</p>
      <p class="relationship__links"><a href="https://techne.institute">techne.institute</a></p>
    </article>

    <article class="relationship">
      <h3>ATLAS Institute &amp; Naropa University</h3>
      <p>We are in deep connection with CU Boulder's ATLAS Institute and with Naropa University — two institutions working at the intersection of technology, arts, and integral learning. Their proximity is not coincidental; we are working to foster the culture that can emerge between them.</p>
      <p class="relationship__links"><a href="https://www.colorado.edu/atlas">colorado.edu/atlas</a> <a href="https://www.naropa.edu">naropa.edu</a></p>
    </article>

    <article class="relationship">
      <h3>Open Civics</h3>
      <p>Working on improving civic processes and protocols — building the open infrastructure that healthy governance requires. We share a belief that civic participation needs better tools and better culture.</p>
      <p class="relationship__links"><a href="https://opencivics.co">opencivics.co</a></p>
    </article>

    <article class="relationship">
      <h3>Community Coordination Tools</h3>
      <p>We are working with organizations in Oakland and beyond on community calendaring and coordination tools — building the practical software that helps people know what's happening and show up for each other.</p>
      <p class="relationship__links"><a href="https://oaklog.org">oaklog.org</a></p>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="newsletter" aria-labelledby="news-h">
  <h2 class="sec__title" id="news-h">Newsletter</h2>
  <div class="sec__body">
    <p>We publish a newsletter weaving together what's happening in our community — events, ideas, and dispatches from the work.</p>
    <p><a href="https://wovenweb.beehiiv.com/subscribe" class="action">Subscribe</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="connect" aria-labelledby="connect-h">
  <h2 class="sec__title" id="connect-h">Connect</h2>
  <div class="sec__body">
    <p>If this work resonates — if you're a potential funder, collaborator, or fellow traveler — we'd love to hear from you.</p>
    <p class="connect__email"><a href="mailto:hello@wovenweb.org">hello@wovenweb.org</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
